<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>'50% savvy political tactics, 50% extraordinarily good luck' - the formula to Meloni's success?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d86cbba3ccf4c331e724e8899a2df3fa11efd647dd4537397d4803a40487455e</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T20:57:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260903-50-savvy-political-tactics-50-extraordinarily-good-luck-the-formula-to-meloni-s-success" /><summary type="html">Giorgia Meloni's hard-right government on Friday becomes the longest-lasting in Italy's postwar history -- a notable record that belies considerable challenges ahead of elections next year. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Nathalie Tocci, Director of the Istituto Affari Internazionali in Rome and Professor of Practice at the John Hopkins University SAIS. She says that Meloni's success comes down to "50 percent savvy political tactics and 50 percent extraordinarily good luck".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Why Ukraine’s drained Kakhovka Dam is strategic for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8e04596d0c523d93d7430259a1904d078a240e95ca6f8ab9552a12988ef3102</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:34:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-why-ukraine-drained-kakhovka-dam-strategic-russia--143f379d846d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-why-ukraine-drained-kakhovka-dam-strategic-russia" /><summary type="html">Small groups of Russian soldiers have been inching forward through the vast, drained Kakhovka reservoir since they blew up the dam in June 2023. Russian forces are infiltrating this “no man’s land” for reconnaissance purposes rather than for a future military offensive, said a military expert.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Giorgia Meloni government becomes Italy's longest-lasting since World War II</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fd3919c2b7e990860376a7c684b7af4884685a1a530e1ad48ce8a16d1f3ae26</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:29:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-giorgia-meloni-government-becomes-italy-s-longest-lasting-since-world-war-ii--f321ed0a24d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-giorgia-meloni-government-becomes-italy-s-longest-lasting-since-world-war-ii" /><summary type="html">Italy's first female Prime Minister, Giorgia Meloni, has surpassed a longevity record set by the late Silvio Berlusconi. When she took office in 2022, many European allies viewed her with unease, given her party's neo-fascist roots. Yet she has governed pragmatically, working within EU institutions and even supporting Ukraine. Domestically, however, she has targeted same-sex parents and clamped down on press freedom.</summary></entry><entry><title>France-UK ties and humour celebrated as London receives Bayeux Tapestry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a62e14a230ae7afdc2fc45a63c3ae4a93a7b6e4d7665f480bcb6a22d3b63c638</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:27:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-uk-ties-and-humour-celebrated-as-london-receives-bayeux-tapestry-1--6ef2090555dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-uk-ties-and-humour-celebrated-as-london-receives-bayeux-tapestry-1" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel #Macron is in #London on the occasion of the #Bayeux Tapestry's exhibition at the #BritishMuseum. The 1,000-year-old work of woven art recounts the Battle of #Hastings, in which William the Conqueror – #KingCharles's ancestor – led the Norman Conquest of #England. An opportunity for the French president, the British PM Andy #Burnham and British monarch to celebrate the strong ties between the two countries.</summary></entry><entry><title>Driverless robotaxis hit the streets of London</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c68390e8de068f2e5915ebc51a17f1c544cb84346551f0aac274b3c53059e45</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:16:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-driverless-robotaxis-hit-the-streets-of-london--2660dfa1427c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-driverless-robotaxis-hit-the-streets-of-london" /><summary type="html">London is entering the era of autonomous vehicles: driverless cabs are now available through Uber and British tech firm Wayve in the capital. It marks a setback for Google's Waymo and Chinese giant Baidu, which have been eyeing Europe as a largely untapped market for autonomous vehicles. But for Wayve, it is its first mass-market rollout, and the company now plans to expand to Tokyo and 10 other cities with Uber.</summary></entry><entry><title>Murder of Daphne Caruana Galizia: Campaigner 'devastated' at tycoon's acquittal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f43d5342d6e82bea40e8d090bf16a392db3f1a0a5f57eaf8397f2431f3e3efb</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/i-m-devastated-by-the-verdict-says-tom-gibson-deputy-dir-for-committee-to-protect-journalists--f0de620fc0ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/i-m-devastated-by-the-verdict-says-tom-gibson-deputy-dir-for-committee-to-protect-journalists" /><summary type="html">A campaigner who has worked on the case of murdered Maltese journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia since she was killed by a car bomb in 2017 has spoken of his devastation at the not guilty verdict.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>France's Macron meets UK PM Burnham at Downing Street</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5b222128b0abc7352d3c3321fdc7b57930e90e59456bace734145b6ab1376d5</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T13:45:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-s-macron-meets-uk-pm-burnham-at-downing-street--e3b95d5ceaa7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-s-macron-meets-uk-pm-burnham-at-downing-street" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron met Britain’s new Prime Minister, Andy Burnham, for official talks at 10 Downing Street. The meeting came a day after the pair were joined by King Charles and Queen Camilla at the British Museum for a preview of the Bayeux Tapestry exhibition in London. Macron is the first EU leader to meet Burnham. Talks are expected to cover relations between Britain and the European Union, support for Ukraine, and migrant crossings in the English Channel.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's Sanchez says no 'solid proof' that Morocco planned Ceuta crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd5822318cffa42dcd37b048923961e42b9504cf98ef1323ee4a489908ce72fe</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T11:58:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-spain-s-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-that-morocco-planned-ceuta-crisis--4482acec72d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-spain-s-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-that-morocco-planned-ceuta-crisis" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez has told lawmakers that there is no evidence the Ceuta migrant crisis was orchestrated by Morocco's government. His remarks come a day after tens of thousands of people took part in protests across the country to criticize his handling of the migrant influx. He acknowledged that Ceuta was both a humanitarian crisis and an administrative challenge. But he rejected the findings of a police report that seemed to lay blame on Morocco. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid, Spain.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin's 'global battle' against US, NATO: Russia 'testing' NATO since 2022 Ukraine invasion began</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3050a0ee47e08d6ef46195f5a5c3fd52460865b5c410bb6344521e419047de36</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T10:26:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260903-putin-s-global-battle-against-us-nato-russia-testing-nato-since-2022-ukraine-invasion-began--62697efb03cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260903-putin-s-global-battle-against-us-nato-russia-testing-nato-since-2022-ukraine-invasion-began" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Anna Borshchevskaya, Senior Fellow at The Washington Institute. She interprets Russia's reported missile support for Iran not as an isolated arms transaction, but as part of a broader geopolitical strategy in which Moscow treats Ukraine, Iran, NATO and the United States as interconnected fronts. In her analysis, Vladimir Putin’s objective is less about pursuing direct military confrontation with Washington than about altering the strategic environment around it: strengthening actors hostile to the United States, increasing the costs of American and Israeli military action, and repeatedly probing Western thresholds for retaliation.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Meloni government sets longevity record in Italy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:573aef53bfbf463a581db149c9b97ff2c1af5e0bd5c78171db71cd78fe6e4e19</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T10:11:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-meloni-government-sets-longevity-record-in-italy--a69c834200f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-meloni-government-sets-longevity-record-in-italy" /><summary type="html">Giorgia Meloni's hard-right government has been in power for 1,413 days. She surpassed the record set by Silvio Berlusconi between 2001 and 2005, making her government Italy's longest serving uninterrupted government since World War II, after a period of intense instability. Italy has had 68 governments in the last 80 years. Giorgia Meloni and her party will celebrate the feat on Friday with a huge pre-election rally in the southern city of Bari. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta tells more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Norway seizes Russian ship to enforce $4.22 billion Ukrainian compensation claim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8de1cfb5bd71c7c063d6fd00501092792d97ea08423f07d806e10300d186ff3b</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T10:07:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-norway-seizes-russian-ship-to-enforce-4-22-billion-ukrainian-arbitration-claim--8ffd5a80a237.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-norway-seizes-russian-ship-to-enforce-4-22-billion-ukrainian-arbitration-claim" /><summary type="html">Norway said Wednesday it had seized a Russian ship as part of a Ukrainian effort to recover $4.22 billion awarded to state energy firm Naftogaz over Russia’s seizure of its assets in Crimea in 2014. The Professor Molchanov vessel was detained off the Arctic Svalbard archipelago after a Norwegian court ordered its arrest.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>No 'solid proof' Morocco planned Ceuta migrant rush, says Spanish PM Sanchez</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4506e0cfcfc145ffa203a75d0136b62ec35906e2bbf4894f550e384841fc58c</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T08:18:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-morocco-planned-ceuta-migrant-rush--1ed53eaa7182.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-morocco-planned-ceuta-migrant-rush" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez said Thursday there was no "solid proof" that Morocco orchestrated a migrant rush into Ceuta in July following the emergence of a police report highlighting multiple failings by Moroccan security forces.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Churchillian moment? Macron in Britain amid scramble to boost European defence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5e78927f35dd29855c5a4ccba877cdd2212c93728fcea41a3b32114efd474ce</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T07:39:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260903-churchillian-moment-macron-in-britain-amid-scramble-to-boost-european-defence--13e2ba2d0940.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260903-churchillian-moment-macron-in-britain-amid-scramble-to-boost-european-defence" /><summary type="html">What can an 11th-century comic strip about the Norman Conquest of England tell us about the spectre of sea change in 2026 Europe? France’s president is on hand for the hottest ticket in London, the first-ever cross-Channel visit of the Bayeux Tapestry, which, for the record, is not a tapestry but a delicate scroll of embroidered cloth that chronicles a radical turning point in our continent’s history. Should France’s outgoing president and the British monarch who welcomes him be likened more to the defending Saxons or the invading Normans?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Macron, Burnham hold talks on migrants, EU after viewing Bayeux Tapestry in London</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8800662b11ba2292ed6dc5af8ffc5e805eefbefc801986d375190c321cca447</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T06:47:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-macron-to-hold-first-talks-with-uk-s-burnham-after-viewing-bayeux-tapestry-in-london--cf8928d0a830.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-macron-to-hold-first-talks-with-uk-s-burnham-after-viewing-bayeux-tapestry-in-london" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham held their first talks on Thursday after meeting a day earlier at the Bayeux Tapestry exhibition at the British Museum. Topping the agenda were several issues, including migrant boats crossing the Channel, British-EU relations and the Ukraine war.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine warns Russian airspace ‘not safe’ in message to UN aviation watchdog</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4519979547313b260718ce7b89f9278a5661d010088033182dd8fade09878402</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T22:46:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-un-civilian-flight-safety-russian-airspace-ukraine--07f316548901.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-un-civilian-flight-safety-russian-airspace-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Ukraine urged the UN aviation agency to call for a full ban on flights through Russian airspace after President Volodymyr Zelensky warned it was becoming unsafe. Kyiv plans increased retaliation against intensified Russian strikes but would target only military facilities, Zelensky said, citing growing Ukrainian drone activity over Russia.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Outrage in Malta as court acquits tycoon in investigative journalist murder case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7d700a76213e3f2d700d6ddb52195ab03d27c2ca79f174e79149c2bdaad3e6b</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T21:56:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-reporter-murder--2cac186cd75a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-reporter-murder" /><summary type="html">A Maltese court on Wednesday acquitted tycoon Yorgen Fenech of orchestrating the 2017 car-bomb killing of investigative journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia, a verdict that drew condemnation from her family and press freedom advocates. Her family said the acquittal denied Caruana Galizia justice, while her son called it a “terrible decision”.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky warns airlines Russian skies not safe due to Ukraine drones</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62c04fe5e6ff0a077cd2d96d7c4650193c1ffcfe9600e93f4dc2daa2ed73b4ba</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T19:32:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/zelensky-warns-airlines-russian-skies-not-safe-due-to-ukraine-drones--0846dc6a9c24.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-warns-airlines-russian-skies-not-safe-due-to-ukraine-drones" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky warned Tuesday that his country's drones would make Russia's airspace "completely unsafe" for the duration of the war, drawing accusations of "state terrorism" from Russian leader Vladimir Putin. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Former British Military Intelligence Officer Philip Ingram explains that Zelensky's warning is addressed to "those international airlines from the Middle East, from South East Asia, China included that are still operating into Moscow" adding that "it's all part of the information war and bringing the overall conflict to the Russian people".</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia blamed for explosive-laden drone found at German airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4961ee2a90494728aef9df5541a0b52e96a4ba3a2a8816d65e0fed6684f02d1b</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:11:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-russia-blamed-for-explosive-laden-drone-found-at-german-airport--a786ed42be94.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-russia-blamed-for-explosive-laden-drone-found-at-german-airport" /><summary type="html">After #Germany blamed #Russia for the explosive-laden #drone found at #Leipzig airport on August 4, #Berlin has introduced new sanctions against #Moscow. Namely, its consulate in #Bonn and the Russian House - a cultural centre thought to be a Russian #spy hub - in #Berlin.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany investigates suspected power substation sabotage, Russia summons German envoy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9e9c27bc2067b39733179cfb530b47815b396bda546993e7d9e0339db042dff</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T13:15:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-germany-ivestigates-suspected-power-substation-sabotage-russia-summons-german-envoy--4853f0a31700.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-germany-ivestigates-suspected-power-substation-sabotage-russia-summons-german-envoy" /><summary type="html">Two incidents that disrupted power distribution systems in Germany are being investigated for sabotage, authorities said Wednesday, while one of them was also being examined for possible terrorism links. Meanwhile Russia said it was summoning Germany's charge d'affaires after Berlin blamed Moscow for last month's attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Drone incident in Germany has ‘hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism’, EU's Kallas says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:981e71fc3119369219c8f309505c0cb2d1e0a5206abeaf444148f6270550653b</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T12:59:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-eu-summons-russia-envoys-eyes-sanctions-after-germany-drone-attack--5007b80aa030.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-eu-summons-russia-envoys-eyes-sanctions-after-germany-drone-attack" /><summary type="html">Last month's incident involving an explosive-laden drone at Leipzig airport bears "all the hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism," EU foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said Wednesday. Germany has blamed Russia for the "hybrid attack". The EU has summoned the Russian envoy, and member states were doing the same, Kallas said.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Macron urges France, UK to forge closer bond as Bayeux Tapestry goes on display in Britain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b50f2bbd40e8130820b73e714d24aae5c8f850745b8a095697a4c5f7a2384779</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T01:27:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-france-s-macron-in-britain-to-help-unveil-bayeux-tapestry--e5685b353904.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-france-s-macron-in-britain-to-help-unveil-bayeux-tapestry" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron called on France and Britain to forge closer ties on Wednesday as he joined King Charles III and Prime Minister Andy Burnham to mark the historic loan of the Bayeux Tapestry to the British Museum. Macron said the two allies could build a bond “as close as the threads” of the 950-year-old artwork, which depicts the Norman conquest of England.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany blames Russia for airport drone incident, hits back with sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17036af734cd82b66b708c51f164f55e9f7a74997948f41262524f6b03dc590d</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T20:58:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/germany-blames-russia-for-airport-drone-incident-hits-back-with-sanctions--4fb45ecf7b0d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/germany-blames-russia-for-airport-drone-incident-hits-back-with-sanctions" /><summary type="html">Germany on Tuesday blamed Russia for an attempted "hybrid attack" involving an explosive-laden drone at a strategic airport last month and announced diplomatic counter-measures. The European Union expressed "full solidarity" with Germany, NATO assured that it would defend its members and countries including Britain, Estonia and Poland offered strong backing. Germany will close Russia's consulate in the former capital Bonn later this month, and cancel the contract for the Russian House, a cultural centre in Berlin, said Foreign Minister Johann Wadephul. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Burnham pledges to restore hope as he makes his House of Commons debut as UK leader</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4038f29dc0d6bdbc82d2d50eecc485b31bce89d29d5964fd70e542fd37e9fe1</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T20:54:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/burnham-pledges-to-restore-hope-as-he-makes-his-house-of-commons-debut-as-uk-leader--37fef2f9fef3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/burnham-pledges-to-restore-hope-as-he-makes-his-house-of-commons-debut-as-uk-leader" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Andy Burnham faced lawmakers in the House of Commons on Tuesday for the first time since becoming U.K. leader six weeks ago, with wars in Europe and the Middle East weighing on his promise to kick-start the economy, ease the cost of living and oversee a radical redistribution of power from London to Britain's regions. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Dr Martin Farr, Senior Lecturer in British Contemporary History at Newcastle University.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany blames Russia for Leipzig airport drone attack, orders Russian consulate closed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f303657f98dc811fbc6a7b0dea93f19a0256d6b71f5970ca99ef5ff09bdd094e</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T17:00:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-germany-blames-russia-for-leipzig-airport-drone-attack-orders-russian-consulate-closed--4237b34f641e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-germany-blames-russia-for-leipzig-airport-drone-attack-orders-russian-consulate-closed" /><summary type="html">Germany's government on Tuesday blamed Russia for an attempted attack at Leipzig/Halle Airport on 4 August using an explosive-laden drone, and announced that it would shut down a Russian consulate among other measures against Moscow. French ​President Emmanuel Macron ​said he supported the ​adoption ‌of ⁠new European sanctions ‌against Russia after the attempted drone attack.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>What to know about the new UK PM's agenda as he faces lawmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c63a1a02c42074197b9eedb6a9e21662c6ce70d182a4342e57c4848d8e4c2e8</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T15:39:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-new-uk-pm-s-agenda-as-he-faces-lawmakers--7159b8695669.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-new-uk-pm-s-agenda-as-he-faces-lawmakers" /><summary type="html">Since taking office on July 20, Burnham has traveled around the country promising to deliver renewed national optimism after the downbeat two-year tenure of his predecessor Keir Starmer. Now, it's time for him to face lawmakers for the first time since he has taken office after an unusually long time without having to do so due to the summer recess. FRANCE 24's Benedicte Paviot tells us what to know from his speech.</summary></entry><entry><title>Replay: UK PM Andy Burnham faces lawmakers for first time since taking office</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e8a000ae8829102ea4f976e5f24b03b8ce4d5ea6268bbc850adc2214b5f1b84</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T15:22:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time-since-taking-office--b2983eb40ac0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time-since-taking-office" /><summary type="html">Rewatch UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham's first speech to parliament since taking office six weeks prior.</summary></entry><entry><title>After 'unprecedented honeymoon', UK PM faces lawmakers for first time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82c4bb37a70692a3ec829330a908f6ddff93e7fb65835278fdaa5323368f44a4</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T15:10:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/after-unprecedented-honeymoon-uk-pm-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time--5c153c598613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/after-unprecedented-honeymoon-uk-pm-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Andy Burnham will face lawmakers in the House of Commons on September 1 for the first time since becoming UK leader six weeks ago. This comes as the wars in Europe and the Middle East weighing on his promise to kick-start the economy and ease the cost of living. Andy Burnham has enjoyed quite a long time without facing lawmakers due to the summer recess. FRANCE 24's Benedicte Paviot tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>At least 12 killed and over a dozen injured in Russian strikes on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f69165273b81801b118a1ac8b95aa96c3a95ef246dd515b46bd468c7cec9e59</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T14:56:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/at-least-12-killed-and-over-a-dozen-injured-in-russian-strikes-on-kyiv--d546607aa696.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/at-least-12-killed-and-over-a-dozen-injured-in-russian-strikes-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Russian air attacks killed 12 people and injured many more in Kyiv and the surrounding region early on September 1, authorities said, marking the sixth straight day of intense strikes on the Ukrainian capital. Those injured three children, just as Ukrainian pupils return to school. In a new tactic, Moscow has sent swarms of new jet-powered drones to ⁠plague Kyiv and nearby areas day and night, killing residents and damaging homes and warehouses.</summary></entry></feed>
